    "problem_statement": "### Bug Report: Indentation Error in `get_parser` Function\n\n**Describe the bug**\n\nThere seems to be an indentation error in the `get_parser` function within the `pipdeptree` module. This error is causing an `IndentationError` when attempting to execute the code, which prevents the module from functioning as expected.\n\n**To Reproduce**\n\nAttempt to run the following code snippet:\n\n```python\nfrom pipdeptree import get_parser\n\nparser = get_parser()\n```\n\nThis will result in an error message similar to the following:\n\n```\nIndentationError: expected an indented block after 'for' statement on line 20\n```\n\n**Expected behavior**\n\nThe `get_parser` function should execute without any indentation errors, allowing the parser to be created successfully.\n\n**Environment info**\n\n- OS: Any\n- Python version: 3.x\n- pipdeptree version: Latest from the repository\n\n**Additional context**\n\nThis issue seems to be related to a missing or incorrect indentation in the `get_parser` function, specifically after a `for` loop. This needs to be corrected to ensure the function executes properly."
